---
title: "Provided Cell Editors"
description: "Overview of the built-in cell editors provided with the $framework Data Grid for common data types."
---

The grid provides several built-in cell editors for common data types. Set `cellEditor` on a column definition to use one, or let [Cell Data Types](./cell-data-types/) assign an appropriate editor automatically.

-   [Text Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-text/) — simple single-line text input; the default editor when none is specified
-   [Large Text Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-large-text/) — multi-line textarea for longer string values
-   [Select Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-select/) — browser-native `select` element for picking from a fixed list
-   [Rich Select Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-rich-select/) {% enterpriseIcon /%} — enhanced drop-down with search, filtering, and custom rendering
-   [Formula Cell Editor](./formula-editor-component/) {% enterpriseIcon /%} — spreadsheet-style formula input

The following cell editors are generally used with [Cell Data Types](./cell-data-types/):

-   [Number Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-number/) — HTML `number` input with optional step and precision controls
-   [Date Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-date/) — date picker for `Date` objects or ISO date strings
-   [Checkbox Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-checkbox/) — boolean toggle using an HTML checkbox

